From 553bc629d111e04c4d5feb156fc71dfe250ce5c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hyunW3 <0176778602@naver.com>
Date: Tue, 2 Jun 2026 22:42:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 15/22] bpebyte: BPEByte br_bt (1.3B) = AU-Net + llama3 BPE
 patching, + milestone downstream eval

BPEByte br_bt is the AU-Net hierarchical model with patch boundaries from llama3 BPE tokens
instead of word/regex, so it is param/FLOP-matched to AU-Net 2 1.3B by construction
(~1.324B params, verified on A100).

- regex_cutting.py: 'bpe*' RegexPool strategy (boundary = last byte of each llama3 BPE
  token, "before_root"/br placement) via RegexArgs.bpe_tokenizer_path; reuses the offline
  level_mask path so the model is unchanged. Plus BPEIncrementalBTParser /
  make_incremental_bt_parser for :bt generation (exact-match to offline boundaries; the
  generator re-pool wiring for free-generation is a follow-up).
- lingua/eval_milestones.py + apps/aunet/train.py + apps/main/train.py: blocking in-process
  HellaSwag/ARC-E (acc_norm) eval at eval_milestones fractions (30/60/90/100%), for ALL apps;
  enabled in aunet/llama/bpebyte configs (async_eval_gpus: null).
- eval.py: all_gather override (fixes lm-eval multi-GPU request padding), nll_per_byte,
  handle_non_serializable on result dumps.
- configs/scripts: bpebyte_br_bt_1.3B.yaml (B200), bpebyte_br_bt_1.3B_a100.yaml (8xA100,
  global batch 192), bpebyte_smoke_a100.yaml, train_bpebyte.sh, train_bpebyte_a100.sh.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
